    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d343">

                <pb facs="0713" n="679" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v15p1/pg679"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">320/11–2552: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Department of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >secret<lb/>niact</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">New
                                York</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1952-11-25T14:38:00-05:00">November 25, 1952—2:38
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Delga 256. Dept pass New Delhi. Sent New Delhi niact 5. Limited distribution.
                    From USUN. Re Korea:</p>
                <p>In further effort to meet Indian position, and in order to make absolute minimum
                    changes in Indian draft, US prepared to agree to accept first sentence revised
                    Indian version<anchor n="1" xml:id="d343-f1"/> as is, amending second to read:
                        <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“If, at the end of a further thirty (30) days, there are any prisoners of
                            war whose return to their homelands has not been effected under the
                            above procedures, or whose future has not been provided for by the
                            Political Conference, the responsibility for their care and disposition
                            shall be transferred to a United Nations agency.”</p></quote></p>
                <pb facs="0714" n="680" xml:id="pg680"/>
                <p>We hope this will lead to success in your efforts with Nehru, Delga 252.<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d343-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d343-f1" n="1" xml:id="d343-f1-content">
                <p>The reference was to the revised version of paragraph 17; for the text, see
                    telegram Delga 246, Nov. 24, <ref target="#pg676">p. 676</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d343-f2" n="2" xml:id="d343-f2-content">
                <p><hi rendition="#italic"><ref target="#d343">Supra</ref></hi>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
